Phase 3 verification report (ADR 0010) - Dead-letter routing

Reduced-prompting mode active: automated-test verification only, no
interactive manual-verification walkthrough.

Automated test command: sbt scalafmtCheck test
Result: 119 passed, 0 failed, 0 errors (pureKafka 22, purerestlib 45,
inventoryService 23, orderService 29). scalafmtCheck clean.

What this proves: a message that fails processing after RetryConfig's
bounded retry budget is exhausted is routed to <topic>-dlq (confirmed via
DeadLetterSuite's fake-publish recording test) instead of raising - so a
consumer built on DeadLetter.guard + StreamSupervisor.supervise never has
one poison message crash/restart the whole stream (Phase 2's supervisor is
for genuine stream-level failures, not per-message ones) or block a
partition indefinitely. Own purekafka.dlq.published metric confirmed via
the otel4s in-memory testkit, same pattern Phase 1's RetrySuite uses.

Design note carried into Phase 4+: DeadLetter deliberately reuses
purekafka.resilience.Retry/Guard internally for its bounded-retry half
instead of a second implementation - the only new logic is the
on-exhaustion action (publish+swallow vs. raise).

This closes the dead-letter-routing third of TD-2.4 (dead-letter routing
across all four Kafka-consuming services) - adoption in each service is
separate, out of scope for this track per spec.md.
